    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Wearable ultrasound patch boosts REM sleep without drugs or surgery",
      "url": "https://sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/08/260806050709.htm",
      "summary": "A new wearable patch may help people reach REM sleep faster and remain there longer without medication or surgery. In a study of 28 participants, the device shortened the time to REM by 43 minutes and extended it by about 16 minutes. Researchers also observed signs of improved stress regulation and changes in brain circuits tied to emotion.",
