          "normalized_title": "Scientists Discover a Hidden Cell Signal That May Explain Congenital Heart Defects",
          "normalized_summary": "Researchers at the University of Copenhagen found that a signaling mechanism in the cells’ ‘antennae’ may help explain why some fetuses develop disease in both the heart and other organs. About two of every 100 babies worldwide are born with congenital heart disease, but the biological processes responsible for these conditions are not fully understood. [...]",
